\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{E}_{1}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we can find the product ${E}_{1}^{-1}{E}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n{E}_{1}^{-1}{E}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 9 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186336635 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dd71abb1-455e-50d0-aae4-082b41821ef1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Inverse of an Elementary 3x3 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c4c9df1-7637-5e2f-ac33-61bed0d95f7f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336637} {:answer/id #uuid "3b60f7a0-a85d-58f9-90ef-0c0cb020a871" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336638} {:answer/id #uuid "6a1c45d5-4afa-5c3d-92bd-9181e6f83d4e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336639} {:answer/id #uuid "a48e4bb0-5067-5785-be1a-2943004b8d16" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336640} {:answer/id #uuid "2b12a96d-ab17-5525-a265-9d165b0fba7f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336641}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6a1c45d5-4afa-5c3d-92bd-9181e6f83d4e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336639} :answer-field/id #uuid "9409fd5e-182f-514d-8e3f-3bd37152355d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336636}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "556c0c09-50a9-5d7e-8a9c-c5b5918c2742" :question/math-academy-id "q-75192" :question/problem "What is the inverse of the elementary matrix \n$B=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{3} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "We write down $B$ and the identity matrix $I$ side-by-side (as shown below) and apply an elementary row operation that transforms the left matrix into the identity matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[B\\,|\\,I\\,] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{3} & 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & {R}_{2}:=3{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe inverse is obtained on the right-hand side of our big matrix after the transformation. Therefore, \n\n$$\n{B}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186336642 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "41954d0a-b8ce-52a0-a2c0-002b0078a37d" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Product Involving an Inverse of an Elementary 3x3 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6a31aaf6-3ed9-5921-98bc-e67aeac51691" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 23 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -9\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336644} {:answer/id #uuid "ab11438b-0014-5b40-be31-a68d91c8fa5a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 23 \\\\ 9 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336645} {:answer/id #uuid "d33dd7c8-2043-5543-a612-b353c54ff1e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 23 \\\\ 9 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336646} {:answer/id #uuid "dcdbdfe8-f6f7-5f00-b210-380b9c57ba24" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 9 & 23 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336647} {:answer/id #uuid "aedceb22-41e3-579b-b6d8-8c4c2ff047cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 9 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336648}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d33dd7c8-2043-5543-a612-b353c54ff1e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 23 \\\\ 9 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336646} :answer-field/id #uuid "f97c8d4e-45fe-5dc5-881b-18005e555f97" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336643}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "9e14159e-0fb2-5f69-8f37-0c75aef035c4" :question/math-academy-id "q-75239" :question/problem "Find the product ${E}_{1}{E}_{2}^{-1}$, where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{E}_{1} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 9 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{E}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -23 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that ${E}_{1}$ and ${E}_{2}$ are both elementary matrices.\n\nFirst, we need to find ${E}_{2}^{-1}.$ We write down ${E}_{2}$ and the identity matrix $I$ side-by-side (as shown below) and apply an elementary row operation that transforms the left matrix into the identity matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[{E}_{2}\\,|\\,I\\,] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -23 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+23{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 & 1 & 23 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{E}_{2}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 23 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we can find the product ${E}_{1}{E}_{2}^{-1}:$ \n\n$$\n{E}_{1}{E}_{2}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 9 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 23 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 23 \\\\ 9 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$"}]}
